INT. PHOTOGRAPHY STUDIO - DAY (1893)

Skylight. Brass camera on a tripod. Velvet backdrop painted with a fake garden.

CORNELIUS BRACKENRIDGE (50s, photographer, black cloth over his head) fusses behind the lens.

On a carved chair, PHILIPPA ASHWORTH (20s, high collar, rigid as a candlestick) holds a bouquet. Beside her stands FENWICK ASHWORTH (60s, her father, top hat, walking stick, mustache like a pair of wings).

CORNELIUS
Perfectly still, Miss Ashworth. Ten seconds.

PHILIPPA
I am always perfectly still.

FENWICK
Philippa, do not speak.

CORNELIUS
Quiet, please.

He removes the lens cap. Counts under his breath.

One.

Two.

Philippa's eye twitches. Fenwick's grip on the cane tightens.

Five.

Six.

A fly lands on Fenwick's nose. He sneers. The fly crawls.

Eight.

Nine.

Philippa's bouquet trembles. A petal drops.

Ten.

Cornelius caps the lens with a flourish.

CORNELIUS (CONT'D)
Splendid.

FENWICK
(exploding)
Cornelius, there was a fly!

CORNELIUS
I saw nothing.

FENWICK
It was on my face!

PHILIPPA
Papa, you blinked. It will be a blur.

Cornelius sighs, lifts the plate holder, and slides in a fresh one.

CORNELIUS
Again, then. Perfectly still.
